        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "80dcca38-b311-53e3-9136-9cb9767f51ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Gaghan, Patrick Massett, John Zinman, Steven Soderbergh\n- Works: Gold, Traffic, Syriana\n- Events: 1993 Bre-X mining scandal\n- Places: Indonesia\n\nFacts:\n- In 1993, the Bre-X mining scandal involved a supposed discovery of a massive gold deposit in the jungles of Indonesia.\n- The 2016 American crime drama film Gold is loosely based on the 1993 Bre-X mining scandal.\n- For legal reasons and to enhance the film's appeal, Gold changed character names and story details from the real Bre-X case.\n- Gold was directed by Stephen Gaghan and written by Patrick Massett and John Zinman.\n- Stephen Gaghan wrote the screenplay for Steven Soderbergh's film Traffic, which was based on a Channel 4 series, and he won the Academy Award for that screenplay.\n- Stephen Gaghan wrote and directed Syriana.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ee1cc87e-859b-5d6c-a951-74d5d4d651c6",
        "text": "Page: Gold (2016 film). Sentence: Gold is a 2016 American crime drama film directed by Stephen Gaghan and written by Patrick Massett and John Zinman.\nPage: Gold (2016 film). Sentence: The film is loosely based on the true story of the 1993 Bre-X mining scandal, when a massive gold deposit was supposedly discovered in the jungles of Indonesia; however, for legal reasons and to enhance the appeal of the film, character names and story details were changed.\nPage: Stephen Gaghan. Sentence: He is noted for writing the screenplay for Steven Soderbergh's film \"Traffic\", based on a Channel 4 series, for which he won the Academy Award, as well as \"Syriana\" which he wrote and directed.",
